Rules:
  [E1] Define explicit mappings for fields.
  [E2] Use appropriate analyzers for text.
  [E3] Use keyword type for exact matches.
  [E4] Use nested type for arrays of objects.
  [E5] Use `_source` to control returned fields.
  [E6] Use pagination with `search_after`.
  [E7] Use index templates for consistency.
  [E8] Use ILM for index lifecycle.

Pros:
  - Full-text search
  - Near real-time
  - Scalable

Cons:
  - Resource intensive
  - Complex tuning
  - Operational overhead

Alternatives:
  - OpenSearch (open source fork)
  - Meilisearch (simpler)
  - Typesense (fast)

State: +

